From: Korri contributors
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: fall back to uncached coherent memory for
 mappable images

Mappable textures (screenshots, readback) ask for
HOST_VISIBLE|HOST_COHERENT|HOST_CACHED memory. panvk exposes no cached
coherent type, so findMemoryType() returned -1 and the allocation used
memory type index ~0u.

Only when that lookup fails, retry without HOST_CACHED. Coherent memory
needs no flush or invalidate, so the result is correct, only slower for
CPU reads. A driver that has a cached coherent type never reaches the
retry; if the retry also finds nothing, behaviour is as before.

Korri-local; not upstream.
---
 src/rendervulkan.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
index 6a9ff302..11ce4e88 100644
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -2450,6 +2450,10 @@ bool CVulkanTexture::BInit( uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t depth, uin
 		.allocationSize = memRequirements.size,
 		.memoryTypeIndex = uint32_t(g_device.findMemoryType(properties, memRequirements.memoryTypeBits)),
 	};
+	// panvk has no HOST_CACHED|HOST_COHERENT type. Coherent memory needs no
+	// flush or invalidate, so uncached coherent memory is correct, only slower.
+	if ( allocInfo.memoryTypeIndex == ~0u && flags.bMappable )
+		allocInfo.memoryTypeIndex = uint32_t(g_device.findMemoryType(properties & ~VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT, memRequirements.memoryTypeBits));
 
 	m_size = allocInfo.allocationSize;
 
